# Wrangler local secrets stub (loaded by `wrangler dev`).
#
# Real secrets for production are managed via `wrangler secret put`.
# Do NOT commit a real .dev.vars file.
#
# Copy this file to .dev.vars and replace placeholders before running
# `wrangler dev`. This file documents local-only secret names;
# production values are supplied by the GitHub Actions production environment.

# Better Auth secret. Generate a 32+ byte random string
# locally; production is supplied by the GitHub Actions production
# environment. Use `wrangler secret put BETTER_AUTH_SECRET` only for
# manual recovery or rotation.
# Required by Better Auth's session signing. See ADR-0009.
# BETTER_AUTH_SECRET="replace-me-with-32-byte-random-string"

# Better Auth base URL (origin of the deployment).
# Local development: http://127.0.0.1:3000
# Production: wired through the companion file `wrangler.production.jsonc`
#   — `pnpm run deploy:production` (= `wrangler deploy -c
#   wrangler.production.jsonc`) pins BETTER_AUTH_URL=https://rebuildup.dev
#   and attaches the custom domain. Do not put the production URL here.
# Better Auth infers baseURL from the incoming request when unset,
# which is fine for local dev but required to be pinned in production
# (cookie domain + trusted origin). See ADR-0009 §8 and ADR-0014.
# BETTER_AUTH_URL="http://127.0.0.1:3000"

# Home self-consumption API key
# (ADR-0011). Local dev: run `pnpm run bootstrap:home-api-key` and
# paste the printed `mk_home_…` value here. Production: the value is
# supplied by the GitHub Actions production environment, and the
# `deploy production` workflow runs
# `scripts/ensure-home-api-key.mjs` to reconcile its hash row in D1
# idempotently. Use `wrangler secret put MY_WEB_2026_CONSUMER_API_KEY`
# only for manual recovery or rotation.
# Required scopes:
#   { reactions: ["read", "write"], access_counter: ["read", "write"] }
# Without this key the home reactions widget + counter tile render a
# disabled state.
# MY_WEB_2026_CONSUMER_API_KEY="mk_home_replace-me"
